---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${meta.title} — ${meta.subtitle} | MetalCrafts`}
  description={meta.excerpt}
  ogImage={meta.ogImage}
>
  <main class="attach-page">
    <!-- =====================================================
         HERO
    ====================================================== -->
    <header class="attach-hero">
      <div class="attach-shell">
        <div class="attach-hero__grid">
          <div class="attach-hero__copy">
            <p class="attach-hero__overline">
              Deep dive 05 · Fixation &amp; delivery
            </p>

            <h1 class="attach-hero__title">
              Attachments
              <span>&amp; Packaging</span>
            </h1>

            <p class="attach-hero__desc">{meta.excerpt}</p>

            <div class="attach-hero__meta">
              <time datetime={toNewsISO(meta.date)}>
                {formatNewsDate(meta.date)}
              </time>
              <span class="attach-hero__dot"></span>
              <span>METALCRAFTS</span>
              <span class="attach-hero__dot"></span>
              <span>Deep dive · 05 of 06</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <figure class="attach-hero__visual">
            <div class="attach-hero__frame">
              <Image
                src={heroShot}
                alt="Packaging and attachment reference"
                loading="eager"
                widths={[720, 1080, 1440]}
                sizes="(max-width: 820px) 100vw, 52vw"
              />
            </div>
            <figcaption>
              <span>Fixation &amp; packaging</span>
              <span>Reference</span>
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- =====================================================
         ARTICLE
    ====================================================== -->
    <section class="attach-article">
      <div class="attach-shell">
        <div class="attach-reading">
          <!-- Desktop contents -->
          <aside class="attach-sidebar" aria-label="Article contents">
            <div class="attach-sidebar__sticky">
              <p class="attach-sidebar__heading">In this deep dive</p>

              <nav class="attach-toc">
                {sections.map((item) => (
                  <a
                    href={`#${item.id}`}
                    class="attach-toc__link"
                    data-toc-link={item.id}
                  >
                    <span class="attach-toc__number">{item.number}</span>
                    <span class="attach-toc__text">{item.title}</span>
                  </a>
                ))}
              </nav>

              <div class="attach-sidebar__note">
                <span class="attach-sidebar__mark">MC</span>
                <div class="attach-sidebar__note-body">
                  <p>
                    Part of the manufacturing guide. Hardware images are being
                    photographed — a dash means the slot is reserved.
                  </p>

                  <a
                    href="/resources/metal-craft-guide"
                    class="attach-sidebar__back"
                  >
                    <span aria-hidden="true">←</span>
                    Back to the full guide
                  </a>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </aside>

          <!-- Body -->
          <article class="attach-content">
            <!-- Mobile contents -->
            <details class="attach-mobile-toc">
              <summary>
                <span>In this deep dive</span>
                <span class="attach-mobile-toc__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </summary>
              <nav aria-label="Mobile article contents">
                {sections.map((item) => (
                  <a href={`#${item.id}`}>
                    <span>{item.number}</span>
                    {item.title}
                  </a>
                ))}
              </nav>
            </details>

            <!-- ---------- THESIS ---------- -->
            <section class="attach-thesis" aria-label="The short answer">
              <span class="attach-thesis__label">The short answer</span>
              <p>
                The attachment decides whether a piece stays on; the packaging
                decides what it is worth when it changes hands. Neither is a
                style choice. Both are decided by three facts that have nothing
                to do with taste: what it is worn on, how often, and where it is
                going to be opened.
              </p>
            </section>

            <!-- ---------- 01 ---------- -->
            <section
              id="decision"
              class="attach-section"
              data-article-section="decision"
            >
              <header class="attach-section__header">
                <span class="attach-section__index">01</span>
                <div>
                  <p class="attach-section__eyebrow">Selection</p>
                  <h2>The attachment is a wear decision</h2>
                </div>
              </header>

              <p>
                Every attachment in this guide answers the same question in a
                different way: how does this piece hold on to something that is
                not part of it? The answer is fixed by three variables, and they
                are all known before a design exists.
              </p>

              <div class="attach-vars">
                {variables.map((item) => (
                  <div class="attach-vars__item">
                    <span class="attach-vars__label">{item.label}</span>
                    <p>{item.text}</p>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>

              <p>
                There is a fourth, quieter variable: what the attachment touches.
                A clutch sits against skin, a keyring against a pocket, a magnet
                against a fridge door. That contact is where compliance starts,
                which is why the last section of this page is not an
                afterthought.
              </p>
            </section>

            <!-- ---------- 02 ---------- -->
            <section
              id="clutches"
              class="attach-section"
              data-article-section="clutches"
            >
              <header class="attach-section__header">
                <span class="attach-section__index">02</span>
                <div>
                  <p class="attach-section__eyebrow">Pins</p>
                  <h2>The four clutches</h2>
                </div>
              </header>

              <p>
                All four do the same job — hold a stem — and differ in how they
                hold, how they release, and how they age. The price difference
                between them is small; the experience difference is not.
              </p>

              <div class="attach-grid">
                {clutches.map((item) => (
                  <div class="attach-item">
                    <div class="attach-item__media">
                      {item.src ? (
                        <Image
                          src={item.src}
                          alt={item.name}
                          width={192}
                          height={192}
                          loading="lazy"
                        />
                      ) : (
                        <span class="attach-item__empty" aria-hidden="true">
                          {item.name
                            .split(" ")
                            .map((word) => word[0])
                            .filter((char) => /[A-Za-z]/.test(char))
                            .join("")
                            .slice(0, 2)}
                        </span>
                      )}
                    </div>
                    <div class="attach-item__body">
                      <h3>{item.name}</h3>
                      <p class="attach-item__zh">{item.zh}</p>
                      <p class="attach-item__note">{item.note}</p>
                      <p class="attach-item__best">{item.best}</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ---------- 03 ---------- -->
            <section
              id="no-clutch"
              class="attach-section"
              data-article-section="no-clutch"
            >
              <header class="attach-section__header">
                <span class="attach-section__index">03</span>
                <div>
                  <p class="attach-section__eyebrow">Pins</p>
                  <h2>When there is no clutch</h2>
                </div>
              </header>

              <p>
                Four ways to mount a piece without a stem and a clutch. They are
                not inferior — they solve cases the clutch cannot, usually where
                weight or garment matters more than unit cost.
              </p>

              <div class="attach-grid">
                {noClutch.map((item) => (
                  <div class="attach-item">
                    <div class="attach-item__media">
                      {item.src ? (
                        <Image
                          src={item.src}
                          alt={item.name}
                          width={192}
                          height={192}
                          loading="lazy"
                        />
                      ) : (
                        <span class="attach-item__empty" aria-hidden="true">
                          {item.name
                            .split(" ")
                            .map((word) => word[0])
                            .filter((char) => /[A-Za-z]/.test(char))
                            .join("")
                            .slice(0, 2)}
                        </span>
                      )}
                    </div>
                    <div class="attach-item__body">
                      <h3>{item.name}</h3>
                      <p class="attach-item__zh">{item.zh}</p>
                      <p class="attach-item__note">{item.note}</p>
                      <p class="attach-item__best">{item.best}</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ---------- 04 ---------- -->
            <section
              id="magnets"
              class="attach-section"
              data-article-section="magnets"
            >
              <header class="attach-section__header">
                <span class="attach-section__index">04</span>
                <div>
                  <p class="attach-section__eyebrow">Fridge magnets</p>
                  <h2>Four ways to hold a magnet</h2>
                </div>
              </header>

              <p>
                On a fridge magnet the magnet is the attachment. The choice is
                governed by weight and by shape: a large flat piece tolerates a
                thin sheet, a small heavy piece does not. A magnet that is too
                weak does not fall off — it slides, which looks worse.
              </p>

              <div class="attach-grid">
                {magnets.map((item) => (
                  <div class="attach-item">
                    <div class="attach-item__media">
                      {item.src ? (
                        <Image
                          src={item.src}
                          alt={item.name}
                          width={192}
                          height={192}
                          loading="lazy"
                        />
                      ) : (
                        <span class="attach-item__empty" aria-hidden="true">
                          {item.name
                            .split(" ")
                            .map((word) => word[0])
                            .filter((char) => /[A-Za-z]/.test(char))
                            .join("")
                            .slice(0, 2)}
                        </span>
                      )}
                    </div>
                    <div class="attach-item__body">
                      <h3>{item.name}</h3>
                      <p class="attach-item__zh">{item.zh}</p>
                      <p class="attach-item__note">{item.note}</p>
                      <p class="attach-item__best">{item.best}</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ---------- 05 ---------- -->
            <section
              id="keychains"
              class="attach-section"
              data-article-section="keychains"
            >
              <header class="attach-section__header">
                <span class="attach-section__index">05</span>
                <div>
                  <p class="attach-section__eyebrow">Keychains</p>
                  <h2>Rings, hooks and chains</h2>
                </div>
              </header>

              <p>
                The charm is the visible part and the ring is the part that gets
                used. Two rules cover most of it: the ring gauge has to match the
                hole, and the fitting has to match what the piece will hang from.
              </p>

              <div class="attach-grid">
                {keychains.map((item) => (
                  <div class="attach-item">
                    <div class="attach-item__media">
                      {item.src ? (
                        <Image
                          src={item.src}
                          alt={item.name}
                          width={192}
                          height={192}
                          loading="lazy"
                        />
                      ) : (
                        <span class="attach-item__empty" aria-hidden="true">
                          {item.name
                            .split(" ")
                            .map((word) => word[0])
                            .filter((char) => /[A-Za-z]/.test(char))
                            .join("")
                            .slice(0, 2)}
                        </span>
                      )}
                    </div>
                    <div class="attach-item__body">
                      <h3>{item.name}</h3>
                      <p class="attach-item__zh">{item.zh}</p>
                      <p class="attach-item__note">{item.note}</p>
                      <p class="attach-item__best">{item.best}</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>

              <p>
                A thin ring on a heavy charm deforms before it breaks, and a
                deformed ring no longer opens cleanly. That failure is almost
                always a specification error, not a wear issue.
              </p>
            </section>

            <!-- ---------- 06 ---------- -->
            <section
              id="cufflinks"
              class="attach-section"
              data-article-section="cufflinks"
            >
              <header class="attach-section__header">
                <span class="attach-section__index">06</span>
                <div>
                  <p class="attach-section__eyebrow">Cufflinks</p>
                  <h2>Cufflinks and tie hardware</h2>
                </div>
              </header>

              <p>
                Cufflink hardware is judged by one thing the buyer does every
                time: putting it on. A mechanism that needs two hands and a
                mirror will be left in the drawer, whatever the face looks like.
              </p>

              <div class="attach-grid">
                {cufflinks.map((item) => (
                  <div class="attach-item">
                    <div class="attach-item__media">
                      {item.src ? (
                        <Image
                          src={item.src}
                          alt={item.name}
                          width={192}
                          height={192}
                          loading="lazy"
                        />
                      ) : (
                        <span class="attach-item__empty" aria-hidden="true">
                          {item.name
                            .split(" ")
                            .map((word) => word[0])
                            .filter((char) => /[A-Za-z]/.test(char))
                            .join("")
                            .slice(0, 2)}
