                      <p class="attach-item__zh">{item.zh}</p>
                      <p class="attach-item__note">{item.note}</p>
                      <p class="attach-item__best">{item.best}</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>

              <p>
                The cost that surprises people here is not the box. It is the
                carton: a rigid box that measures 90 mm on each side takes four
                times the volume of a carded pin, so the freight per unit rises
                even when the box itself is cheap.
              </p>
            </section>

            <!-- ---------- 09 ---------- -->
            <section
              id="pack-detail"
              class="attach-section"
              data-article-section="pack-detail"
            >
              <header class="attach-section__header">
                <span class="attach-section__index">09</span>
                <div>
                  <p class="attach-section__eyebrow">Details</p>
                  <h2>Details that decide quality</h2>
                </div>
              </header>

              <p>
                Two suppliers can quote the same “printed backing card” and hand
                over different objects. The difference is in five numbers, none
                of which appear in a photograph.
              </p>

              <div class="attach-specs">
                {packDetails.map((item) => (
                  <div class="attach-spec">
                    <span class="attach-spec__label">{item.label}</span>
                    <p>{item.text}</p>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>

              <p>
                The hole is the one worth arguing about. A card hole a fraction
                too large lets the pin rotate under its own weight, so the face
                sits at an angle on every peg — and the fix is a new die for the
                card, not a new print file.
              </p>
            </section>

            <!-- ---------- 10 ---------- -->
            <section
              id="compliance"
              class="attach-section"
              data-article-section="compliance"
            >
              <header class="attach-section__header">
                <span class="attach-section__index">10</span>
                <div>
                  <p class="attach-section__eyebrow">Compliance</p>
                  <h2>Nickel, lead, and what to ask for</h2>
                </div>
              </header>

              <p>
                Compliance is not a document you attach at the end. It is a
                property of the part, and the part is decided by the attachment
                and the plating — the two things that touch skin.
              </p>

              <div class="attach-compliance">
                {compliance.map((item) => (
                  <div class="attach-compliance__row">
                    <h3>{item.label}</h3>
                    <p>
                      <span>Market</span>
